    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That distinction between \"covenant\" and \"contract-based secular relationships\" is a really insightful point. It almost sounds like you're saying secularism is fundamentally less capable of creating true social cohesion. If we look at the increasing fragmentation in modern secular societies, would it be accurate to conclude that the decline of religious institutions is a primary driver of social instability?",
